WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.112
The method builds on spin-weighted spherical CNNs.

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:08.218
Its centerpiece is a set of new components that all
live in the spectral domain.

00:00:08.298 --> 00:00:13.836
A phase collapse nonlinearity takes the modulus of
the features to collapse their phase,

00:00:13.916 --> 00:00:19.198
which restores rotation invariance while losing no
information in the nonzero spins.

00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:23.793
Batch normalization and pooling are also moved into
the spectral domain,

00:00:23.873 --> 00:00:29.283
and the residual block adds its skip connection
directly between Fourier coefficients.

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.007
On the implementation side,

00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:38.092
the authors compute the Fourier transforms as dense
matrix multiplications rather than fast Fourier transforms,

00:00:38.172 --> 00:00:44.220
because on TPUs matrix multiplies are extremely
fast while memory reshuffling is the bottleneck.
